10 19-P:2-a AdvisoryCouncilontheSystemofCareforHealthAginginNewHampshire.
11 I. Thecommissionshallestablishanadvisorycouncilonthesystemofcareforhealthyaging
12 inNewHampshire. Thepurposeoftheadvisorycouncilshallbeto:
13 (a) Improvethewell-beingofolderadultsandcaregivers;
14 (b) Identify cost-savings and opportunities to increase collaboration, efficiency, and the
15 effectivenessoftheservicearrayandservicedeliverysystem;and
16 (c) Assist and advise the commissioner of the department of health and human services
17 onthesystemofcareprinciplesandvaluesandimplementationofRSA151-E:22through151-E:27.
18 II.(a) The director of the division of long-term supports and services, or the director's
19 designee, and one member of the state commission on aging shall serve as the permanent co-
20 chairpersonsoftheadvisorycouncil.
21 (b) Additional members of the advisory council representing diverse perspectives shall
22 be appointed by the commission on aging and shall include older adults and family caregivers with
23 relevant experience, members of agencies serving older adults including public, private, consumer
24 advocacy,andnon-profitorganizations,andindividualswithrelevantpolicyexpertise.
25 III. Theadvisorycouncilshallmeetatleastquarterlyandmaymeetmoreoftenatthecallof
26 thecommission.
27 IV. The duties of the council shall include reviewing and making recommendations
28 regardingallaspectsoftheimplementationofthesystemofcareforhealthyagingestablishedunder
29 RSA 151-E:22 through 151-E:27. Such duties shall also include addressing the availability of long
30 term supports and services for individuals across the continuum of care, including but not be limited
31 to:
